            <ArticleTitle>Annual increase in body mass index in children with asthma on higher doses of inhaled steroids.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>549-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>There is a greater annual increase in body mass index in children with asthma receiving inhaled steroids at a dose &gt; or =400 microg/day (0.5 kg/m2/year; n=100) compared with those receiving &lt; or =200 microg/day (0.1 kg/m2/year; n=98) (P=.0003). This is consistent with an annual increase in body fat in children with asthma receiving &gt; or =400 microg/day of inhaled steroids.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
